CONTRACTS
[~] APIRegistry.sol
[~] X402Facilitator.sol
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOG
* Created init APIRegistry.sol & APIRegistry.t.sol
    FUNC:
    - register API endpoints
    - store API metadata on-chain
    - list all registered APIs
    - query APIs by provider
    - update API pricing/status
    - query API details
    - active/inactive API checks
    - utility helpers (total APIs, provider mappings)
    - event emission for indexing/frontend tracking
    ADDED:
    - NatSpec documentation/comments
    - API lifecycle documentation
    - APIDeactivated event
    - clearer discovery layer architecture
    - provider/API mapping explanations
    - usage flow comments for agents/providers
    LACK:
    - payment enforcement
    - x402 settlement linkage
    - API access validation
    - ownership transfer/admin controls
    - endpoint ownership verification
    - categories/tags indexing
    - staking/reputation system
* Created init X402Facilitator.sol & X402Facilitator.t.sol
    FUNC:
    - accept payment intent via settle()
    - verifies off-chain signature (basic ECDSA auth)
    - transfers USDC via ERC20 transferFrom()
    - splits payment (provider + treasury fee)
    - prevents replay attacks using nonce tracking
    - enforces deadline expiration
    - emits PaymentSettled event for indexing
    LACK:
    - no native EIP-3009 (transferWithAuthorization) support
    - no full EIP-712 typed data structure
    - relies on ERC20 allowance (approve() required once)
    - simplified cryptographic binding (custom hash scheme)
    - no on-chain authorization state validation (true USDC flow)
- Still TODO: X402Facilitator and APIRegistry improvements
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GETTING STARTED
- after cloning this repository, run the following steps:
    1. Move into contracts folder
            cd packages/contracts
    2. Install Foundry dependencies (IMPORTANT)
            forge install
        2.1. This installs forge-std into:
                lib/forge-std
        2.2. If imports fail, run:
                forge install foundry-rs/forge-std
    3. Build contracts
            forge build
    4. Run tests
            forge test -vv
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLEAN SETUP 
- if something breaks
    If forge-std is corrupted:
            rm -rf lib
            forge install
    If cache issues occur:
            forge clean
            forge build
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOCAL BLOCKCHAIN TESTING (ANVIL)
    1. Start local chain
            anvil
    This runs at:
            http://127.0.0.1:8545
    It also prints private keys you can use for testing.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEPLOYMENT FLOW (LOCAL)
    1. Build contracts
            forge build
    2. Deploy using script
            forge script script/Deploy.s.sol \
            --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545 \
            --private-key <ANVIL_PRIVATE_KEY> \
            --broadcast
    This will:
        - compile contracts
        - execute Deploy.s.sol
        - deploy APIRegistry + X402Facilitator
        - print contract addresses
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MANUAL TESTING (CAST)
    Register API
            cast send <REGISTRY_ADDRESS> \
            "registerAPI(string,string,uint256)" \
            "BTC API" \
            "https://api.com" \
            1000 \
            --private-key <PRIVATE_KEY> \
            --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545
    Get API
            cast call <REGISTRY_ADDRESS> \
            "getAPI(bytes32)" <API_ID>
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BUILD / TEST COMMANDS
    1. Compile
            forge build
    2. Run tests
            forge test
    3. Verbose tests
            forge test -vv
    4. Very verbose (debug)
            forge test -vvvv
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT STRUCTURE
    src/
          APIRegistry.sol      => API discovery => pricing layer
          X402Facilitator.sol  => payment verification => settlement layer
    test/
          APIRegistry.t.sol    => unit tests for registry
    script/
          Deploy.s.sol         => deployment automation
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WORKFLOW SUMMARY
1. anvil
2. forge install
3. forge build
4. forge test
5. forge script Deploy.s.sol --broadcast
6. cast send / cast call (manual testing)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTES
- forge-std is required for tests and scripts
- All tests run locally in memory (no real blockchain needed)
- Deployment only required for integration or Morph testnet
